findings.body:
The diff removes `ghost/i18n/locales/zh/comments.json` entirely (74 lines). The PR description says this file was refined for consistent 评论/名字 terms and clearer load/show hints. Checked at head `6eb367b`: the file does not exist, while every other locale directory still has a `comments.json`. The Chinese comments widget therefore loses all of its zh-authored strings, including "Load more", "Show {amount} more replies", "Reply", and "Sign in".

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/comments.json" lines="1-74"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The intent in the description and the diff disagree. Either the file was deleted by mistake when the branch was generated, or the deletion is intentional and the description is wrong. Either way the author needs to confirm before merge.

::

The English source is `{memberEmail} will no longer receive {newsletterName} newsletter.` The new zh value drops `{newsletterName}` entirely: "{memberEmail}将不会再收到新闻信。" The old value kept it. A member who unsubscribes from one of several newsletters now sees a message that doesn't say which one, which is a user-visible loss of information. Translators shouldn't drop interpolation variables just to make the sentence shorter.

::diff{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="9-9"}

::suggestion{file="ghost/i18n/locales/zh/portal.json" lines="9-9"}
"{memberEmail}将不会再收到{newsletterName}新闻信。": "{memberEmail}将不会再收到{newsletterName}新闻信。"
